---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: The Interdependency WebMCP
description: Full skill-lib catalogue, browser-native handoff, and explicit MCP tool invocation.
permalink: /webmcp/
webmcp: true
---
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="webmcp-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">WebMCP Challenge · live public surface</p>
  <h1 id="webmcp-title">The Interdependency WebMCP</h1>
  <p><strong>The page is the provider.</strong> Human and browser agent use the same repository identity and skill material. The human chooses a repository, chooses how the agent should work in that repository, and states the desired outcome; Send exposes that exact handoff to the browser agent.</p>
  <p><strong>Remote MCP registry:</strong> <code>https://the-interdependency-mcp.onrender.com/mcp</code></p>
  <p><a href="https://the-interdependency-mcp.onrender.com/health">Open remote MCP health check</a></p>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="webmcp-status-title">
  <h2 id="webmcp-status-title">LIVE</h2>
  <p data-webmcp-status data-state="hmmm">Loading the commit-pinned skill registry and checking browser WebMCP support…</p>
  <p data-remote-mcp-status data-state="hmmm">Checking remote MCP health…</p>
  <p><strong>Skill source:</strong> <span data-webmcp-source>resolving…</span></p>
  <p><strong>Repository projection:</strong> {{ generated.repos.publicRepoCount }} active public repositories</p>
  <noscript><p>JavaScript is disabled, so browser WebMCP registration and the human-to-agent handoff cannot run. The skill and repository catalogues remain readable.</p></noscript>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="repository-target-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Shared human + agent repository material</p>
  <h2 id="repository-target-title">1. Choose the repository</h2>
  <p>The repository establishes the agent's working context before any action or skill is selected. The list is generated from the current active public repositories in <code>The-Interdependency</code>, and the selected repository's exact observed default-branch head travels with the handoff. Selection grants no write permission.</p>
  <label for="human-repository-target">Target repository</label>
  <select id="human-repository-target" data-human-repository-target>
    <option value="">Choose a repository…</option>
    {% for repo in generated.repos.repositories %}
    <option
      value="{{ repo.name }}"
      data-repository-url="{{ repo.html_url }}"
      data-repository-head="{{ repo.head_sha or '' }}"
      data-repository-branch="{{ repo.default_branch or '' }}"
      data-repository-status="{{ repo.status or '' }}"
      data-repository-category="{{ repo.category or '' }}"
    >{{ repo.name }}{% if repo.category %} — {{ repo.category }}{% endif %}</option>
    {% endfor %}
  </select>
  <div class="hmmm-boundary">
    <strong>Selected repository</strong>
    <span data-selected-repository>No repository selected.</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="skill-catalog-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Shared human + agent skill material</p>
  <h2 id="skill-catalog-title">2. Choose how the agent should work</h2>
  <p data-skill-stage-status data-state="hmmm" aria-live="polite">Choose a repository first to enable its agent-work choices.</p>
  <p>All {{ generated.skillRegistry.skills.length }} skills in the verified skill-lib registry are listed below. This is a commit-pinned readout, not a second definition. A skill describes how an authorized agent should work; being listed does not prove an executor is connected.</p>

  <form data-human-skill-filter-form>
    <label for="human-skill-filter">Optional skill search</label>
    <input id="human-skill-filter" data-human-skill-filter name="skill-filter" type="search" placeholder="Search names, definitions, dependencies…" autocomplete="off">
    <span aria-live="polite" data-human-skill-count>{{ generated.skillRegistry.skills.length }} registered skills</span>
  </form>

  {% for group in [{ "kind": "metadata-block", "heading": "Metadata skills" }, { "kind": "procedural", "heading": "Procedural skills" }] %}
  <h3>{{ group.heading }}</h3>
  <div class="grid" data-human-skill-catalog data-skill-group="{{ group.kind }}">
    {% for skill in generated.skillRegistry.skills %}
    {% if skill.kind == group.kind %}
    <article class="card" data-human-skill data-skill-name="{{ skill.name }}" data-skill-kind="{{ skill.kind }}">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ group.kind }}</p>
      <h4>{{ skill.human_title or skill.name }}</h4>
      <p>{{ skill.name }}</p>
      <details data-skill-description>
        <summary>Description</summary>
        <p>{{ skill.description }}</p>
        {% if skill.depends_on and skill.depends_on.length %}
        <p>Required skills: {{ skill.depends_on | join(", ") }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </details>
      <p><button type="button" data-select-skill aria-pressed="false" disabled>Select this skill</button></p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/{{ generated.skillRegistry.source.repository }}/blob/{{ generated.skillRegistry.source.commit }}/{{ skill.path }}">Read canonical skill definition</a></p>
    </article>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

  <div class="hmmm-boundary" data-selected-skill-boundary>
    <strong>Selected skill</strong>
    <span data-selected-skill>No skill selected.</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="human-handoff-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Human → browser agent</p>
  <h2 id="human-handoff-title">3. State the outcome and send</h2>
  <p><button type="button" data-selected-action="inspect" disabled>Inspect selected skill</button> <button type="button" data-selected-action="closure" disabled>Show required skill set</button></p>

  <form data-human-handoff-form>
    <label for="human-handoff-intent"><strong>What do you want the agent to change or produce?</strong></label>
    <textarea id="human-handoff-intent" data-human-handoff-intent name="intent" rows="5" maxlength="4000" placeholder="Describe the desired outcome in ordinary language. The selected repository is carried automatically."></textarea>
    <p><button type="submit" data-human-handoff-send disabled>Send repository + skill + request to agent</button></p>
    <p data-human-handoff-status data-state="hmmm" aria-live="polite">Choose a repository first, then a skill. Nothing is sent merely by selecting or typing.</p>
  </form>

  <pre tabindex="0" data-webmcp-output>Select a repository first, then a skill. No internal repository or skill identifier needs to be typed.</pre>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="mcp-invocation-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Explicit tool invocation · live MCP response</p>
  <h2 id="mcp-invocation-title">4. Connect and call the MCP server</h2>
  <p>The public Interdependency MCP server provides read-only registry tools. To enact a skill, connect an authorized Streamable HTTP MCP executor that actually advertises <code>tiw_execute_skill</code>. The website never invents an execution result or supplies execution authority.</p>
  <p>Only use an MCP endpoint you trust. Browser requests go directly to that endpoint; it must allow your browser origin and return JSON MCP responses. A private VM service requires its own approved gateway or client connection.</p>
  <label for="mcp-endpoint">MCP endpoint</label>
  <input id="mcp-endpoint" data-mcp-endpoint type="url" value="https://the-interdependency-mcp.onrender.com/mcp" autocomplete="url" spellcheck="false">
  <label for="mcp-bearer">Optional bearer token (kept only in this page's memory)</label>
  <input id="mcp-bearer" data-mcp-bearer type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Only for a trusted, authenticated MCP server">
  <p><button type="button" data-mcp-discover>Discover live MCP tools</button></p>
  <p data-mcp-tool-status data-state="hmmm" aria-live="polite">No MCP tools discovered. The public server can be queried without a credential.</p>
  <label for="mcp-tool">Advertised tool</label>
  <select id="mcp-tool" data-mcp-tool disabled><option value="">Discover tools first…</option></select>
  <label for="mcp-arguments">Tool arguments (JSON object)</label>
  <textarea id="mcp-arguments" data-mcp-arguments rows="5" spellcheck="false">{}</textarea>
  <p>
    <button type="button" data-mcp-call disabled>Call selected MCP tool</button>
    <button type="button" data-mcp-enact disabled>Enact selected skill via MCP</button>
  </p>
  <p data-mcp-execution-status data-state="hmmm" aria-live="polite">Skill execution requires a live executor that advertises tiw_execute_skill, a selected repository and skill, and a stated outcome.</p>
  <pre tabindex="0" data-mcp-tool-result>Live MCP results and explicit failures appear here.</pre>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="webmcp-boundary-title">
  <h2 id="webmcp-boundary-title">Same material, meaningful human selection</h2>
  <pre tabindex="0">current public repository projection + skill definitions
                 ↓
human chooses repository + reads the applicable skill
                 ↓
          explicit SEND
                 ↓
       one read-only handoff
                 ↓
agent receives the exact repository, skill set, and human request
                 ↓
agent's separately authorized change tools</pre>
  <p>For fresh-making, choosing the skill supplies an editable standard request. For EPAC selection/display, the human supplies a target and presentation; a repository selection does not select canon. The browser-agent handoff remains read-only and page-session-only. A separate deliberate MCP execution request may invoke an authenticated tool on a connected executor, whose response and authorization remain the executor's responsibility.</p>
</section>

<div class="hmmm-boundary"><strong>hmmm</strong><span>The default public MCP endpoint has no skill executor. Discovering or selecting a skill cannot run it: execution is blocked until an independently authorized MCP service exposes the exact execution tool. Repository observations and skill documentation remain provenance, not credentials or proof of operational capability.</span></div>
